{"task_id": "HumanEval/63", "solution": "```python\ndef fibfib(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the FibFib number sequence using an iterative approach.\n    Handles base cases for n=0, 1, 2 and applies the recurrence relation for n > 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize a list to store fibfib numbers\n    # dp[i] will store fibfib(i)\n    dp = [0] * (n + 1)\n    dp[0] = 0\n    dp[1] = 0\n    dp[2] = 1\n\n    # Compute fibfib(i) for i from 3 up to n\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        dp[i] = dp[i-1] + dp[i-2] + dp[i-3]\n\n    return dp[n]\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/65", "solution": "```python\ndef circular_shift(x, shift):\n    \"\"\"Circular shift the digits of the integer x, shift the digits right by shift\n    and return the result as a string.\n    If shift > number of digits, return digits reversed.\n    \"\"\"\n    x_str = str(x)\n    num_digits = len(x_str)\n\n    if num_digits == 0:\n        return \"\"\n\n    if shift > num_digits:\n        return x_str[::-1]\n    else:\n        effective_shift = shift % num_digits\n        return x_str[-effective_shift:] + x_str[:-effective_shift]\n```"}
