{"task_id": "HumanEval/118", "solution": "```python\ndef get_closest_vowel(word):\n    \"\"\"Finds the closest vowel that stands between two consonants from the right side of the word.\n    Vowels in the beginning and ending don't count.\"\"\"\n\n    VOWELS_LOWERCASE = {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'}\n\n    def is_vowel_char(char: str) -> bool:\n        return char.lower() in VOWELS_LOWERCASE\n\n    def is_consonant_char(char: str) -> bool:\n        # Assumes char is an English letter as per constraints.\n        return char.isalpha() and not is_vowel_char(char)\n\n    n = len(word)\n    if n < 3:\n        return \"\"\n\n    # Iterate from the second-to-last character (index n-2) down to the second character (index 1).\n    # This range ensures that for any 'i', word[i-1] and word[i+1] exist, covering the \"between two consonants\" and \"not at beginning/end\" conditions.\n    for i in range(n - 2, 0, -1):\n        current_char = word[i]\n        prev_char = word[i - 1]\n        next_char = word[i + 1]\n\n        if (is_vowel_char(current_char) and\n            is_consonant_char(prev_char) and\n            is_consonant_char(next_char)):\n            return current_char\n\n    return \"\"\n```"}
