{"task_id": "HumanEval/132", "solution": "```python\ndef is_nested(string):\n    '''\n    Checks if the string contains a valid nested subsequence of brackets, i.e., '[[]]'.\n    Searches for the characters of '[[]]' in sequential order within the input string.\n    '''\n    idx1 = string.find('[', 0)\n    if idx1 == -1:\n        return False\n\n    idx2 = string.find('[', idx1 + 1)\n    if idx2 == -1:\n        return False\n\n    idx3 = string.find(']', idx2 + 1)\n    if idx3 == -1:\n        return False\n\n    idx4 = string.find(']', idx3 + 1)\n    if idx4 == -1:\n        return False\n\n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/130", "solution": "```python\ndef tri(n):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the first n + 1 numbers of the Tribonacci sequence.\n    This function uses memoization to efficiently compute values based on the recurrence relations.\n    \"\"\"\n    memo = {}\n\n    def _get_tri_value(k):\n        \"\"\"A helper function to compute the k-th Tribonacci number with memoization.\"\"\"\n        if k in memo:\n            return memo[k]\n\n        if k == 0:\n            result = 1\n        elif k == 1:\n            result = 3\n        elif k % 2 == 0:  # k is even\n            result = 1 + k / 2\n        else:  # k is odd\n            result = _get_tri_value(k - 1) + _get_tri_value(k - 2) + _get_tri_value(k + 1)\n\n        memo[k] = result\n        return result\n\n    sequence = []\n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        sequence.append(_get_tri_value(i))\n\n    return sequence\n```"}
